# L4 Milestone List

`memory-bank/active/milestones.md` is the L4 plan and state tracker.

1. **In-flight signal**: its presence tells `/niko` that an L4 project is active.
2. **State tracker**: the checklist records which milestones are complete.

Put requirements in `memory-bank/active/projectbrief.md`. Put sequence, invariants, done, and risks in this file.

## File Format

```markdown
# Milestones: <task-id>

## Cross-milestone invariants & constraints

[Properties no milestone may violate. If two milestones share an artifact, state who may touch it and when.]

## Execution Order

[Optional Mermaid flowchart. Omit if all milestones are sequential.]

- [ ] <Deliverable. Include an existing ticket id or URL if one exists.>
- [ ] <Deliverable>
- [ ] <Deliverable>

## Per-milestone done and risks

### <exact checkbox text>
- Done: <what shipped looks like>
- Risks: <what this sub-run must not lose, or "see invariants">
```

Rules:
- Header: `# Milestones: <task-id>` matching the task ID in `memory-bank/active/tasks.md`
- One GFM checkbox per milestone (`- [ ]` or `- [x]`). No sub-bullets. No second sentence. No file lists.
- Do not create tickets. If a ticket already exists, put its id or URL on that checkbox line.
- Only the Execution Order checklist may use `- [ ]` / `- [x]`. Those markers are the milestone list.
- The checklist is serial-safe: walking it one at a time never requires a later milestone.
- When the work is not a straight line, the flowchart shows which milestones may run in parallel. One-at-a-time follows the list. Parallel follows the DAG. The two must agree so a switch mid-project does not conflict.
- The flowchart is not a milestone.

## What Makes a Good Milestone

Each milestone must satisfy all of these:

- **Independently deliverable** — plan, build, test, and commit with no need for a later milestone
- **L1/L2/L3 scoped** — not itself L4
- **Concrete** — names the deliverable ("Add user authentication flow", not "Work on auth")
- **Non-overlapping** — no two milestones do the same work to the same files
- **Done** — the heading block (or a covering invariant) states what shipped looks like

If a milestone fails these, split, merge, or rewrite it before sub-runs begin.

## Lifecycle

| Event | Who | Action |
|-------|-----|--------|
| L4 Plan phase | `.cursor/skills/shared/niko/references/level4/level4-plan.md` | Creates `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` |
| `/niko` re-entry - sub-run complete | `/niko` Step 2a (Advance L4 Milestone) | Checks off the completed milestone (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) |
| `/niko` re-entry - unchecked remain | `/niko` Step 2a → Step 7 (Classify) | Classifies first unchecked as L1/L2/L3, initiates sub-run |
| `/niko` re-entry - all `- [x]` | `/niko` Step 2a | Routes to capstone archive |
| Capstone archive | `.cursor/skills/shared/niko/references/level4/level4-archive.md` | Deletes `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` |

🚨 **Do not create or modify `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` outside of these lifecycle events.** Its presence is a binary signal for `/niko`. A manual create will send the next `/niko` into L4 routing.
